---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import FAQ from '../components/FAQ.astro';
import RelatedLinks from '../components/RelatedLinks.astro';
const faqItems = [
  { question: 'Is Meta Muse free?', answer: 'Yes, with a weekly usage limit. Paid plans are Power ($20/month) and Maximum ($100/month).' },
  { question: 'What is the difference between $20 and $100?', answer: 'Power includes 500M Muse tokens per week. Maximum includes 3B Muse tokens per week.' },
  { question: 'Where do I subscribe?', answer: 'In the Muse mobile app or at muse.ai, signed in with a Meta account. Muse and its subscriptions are in limited testing and are not available everywhere.' },
  { question: 'Can I buy more tokens without upgrading?', answer: 'Yes. Meta documents one-time purchases of additional Muse tokens after you reach a free limit. Subscribers can also buy tokens on top of their weekly allowance.' },
  { question: 'Do Muse tokens expire?', answer: 'Extra purchased tokens do not expire, including after cancellation. Unused weekly subscription allowance does not roll over from a previous billing cycle.' },
  { question: 'Can I cancel my subscription?', answer: 'Yes. Manage your subscription in Settings using the platform and account you subscribed with. Benefits continue until the current billing cycle ends; refunds are not generally provided unless required by law.' },
];
const relatedLinks = [
  { label: 'Buy additional Muse tokens', href: '/buy-additional-muse-tokens/', description: 'One-time top-ups, expiry, and purchase steps.' },
  { label: 'Cancel or manage a Muse subscription', href: '/cancel-manage-muse-subscription/', description: 'Settings, app-store billing, and what happens after cancellation.' },
  { label: 'How to use Meta Muse', href: '/how-to-use-meta-muse/', description: 'Access, Connectors, and permissions.' },
  { label: 'Meta Muse review', href: '/meta-muse-review/', description: 'Capabilities, limitations, and privacy.' },
];
---
<Base title="Meta Muse Pricing: Free, Power $20 & Maximum $100" description="Compare Meta Muse Free, Power ($20/month, 500M tokens/week), and Maximum ($100/month, 3B/week). Subscription access, extra tokens, and cancellation." canonicalPath="/meta-muse-pricing/" pageType="article" breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Meta Muse Pricing' }]}>
  <article class="content">
    <p class="eyebrow">Pricing guide</p>
    <h1>Meta Muse Pricing</h1>
    <p class="lede">Meta Muse has a free tier with a usage limit, plus two paid plans: Power and Maximum. You can subscribe in the Muse mobile app or at <a href="https://muse.ai/">muse.ai</a>. Muse and Muse subscriptions are in limited testing and are not available in every location.</p>
    <section aria-labelledby="free-heading">
      <h2 id="free-heading">Is Meta Muse Free?</h2>
      <p>Yes. Muse is available for free with a weekly usage limit. If you reach that limit, Meta says you can upgrade, wait for the free limit to refresh, or buy additional Muse tokens.</p>
      <p>Media reports around launch cited a free weekly allowance of up to 100 million tokens. Treat that figure as reported commentary unless Meta shows the same number in your account; it is not the official free allowance in the table below.</p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="plans-heading">
      <h2 id="plans-heading">Meta Muse Plans Compared</h2>
      <div class="table-scroll"><table>
        <caption>Meta Muse prices and official weekly usage allowances</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Plan</th><th scope="col">Price</th><th scope="col">Weekly usage (official)</th><th scope="col">Best for</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">Free</th><td>$0</td><td>Limited free weekly usage</td><td>Trying Muse and occasional tasks</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Power</th><td>$20 / month</td><td>500M Muse tokens per week</td><td>Regular weekly use</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Maximum</th><td>$100 / month</td><td>3B Muse tokens per week</td><td>Heavy, ongoing task use</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table></div>
      <p>Weekly usage allowance increases as you upgrade. Exact benefits can vary by region and account; confirm what your account shows during onboarding. Source: <a href="https://www.meta.com/help/subscriptions/1021145227643680/">Meta Help: About Muse subscriptions</a>.</p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="tokens-heading">
      <h2 id="tokens-heading">Additional Muse Tokens</h2>
      <p>After you hit a free or plan limit, you can buy additional Muse tokens in the Muse app or on muse.ai. Meta says:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Extra purchased tokens do not expire, including after you cancel a subscription.</li>
        <li>Unused weekly allowance from a subscription does not roll over from a previous billing cycle.</li>
        <li>Additional tokens have no cash value and cannot be transferred or refunded except where required by law.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>See <a href="/buy-additional-muse-tokens/">how to buy additional Muse tokens</a> and <a href="https://www.meta.com/help/subscriptions/28153473374286914/">Meta’s additional-token documentation</a>.</p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="product-scope-heading">
      <h2 id="product-scope-heading">These Plans Are for the Muse Personal Agent</h2>
      <p>Muse Code is a separate developer subscription with Everyday Usage, High Usage, Power Usage,
        and Maximum Usage plans. Do not apply this page’s Power / Maximum weekly allowances to Muse Code
        or assume they define Muse Image / Muse Video benefits.
        <a href="/what-is-meta-muse/#product-names-heading">Compare product names</a> or read
        <a href="https://dev.meta.ai/docs/muse-code/subscriptions">Muse Code subscription documentation</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="fits-heading">
      <h2 id="fits-heading">Who Each Plan Fits</h2>
      <h3>Free</h3><p>Best when you want to test whether Muse can finish your kind of web task before paying.</p>
      <h3>Power ($20/month)</h3><p>A fit if you expect steady weekly use and the 500M-token allowance covers your workflow.</p>
      <h3>Maximum ($100/month)</h3><p>Makes sense when Muse is a frequent work tool and you need the larger 3B weekly allowance.</p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="check-heading">
      <h2 id="check-heading">What to Check Before You Pay</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Availability in your country: limited testing means Muse is not everywhere yet.</li>
        <li>The plan details shown in your own Muse account.</li>
        <li><a href="/cancel-manage-muse-subscription/">How to manage or cancel the subscription</a> in Settings.</li>
        <li>Whether you need Connectors, such as Gmail or Calendar, for the tasks you care about.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <FAQ items={faqItems} />
    <RelatedLinks links={relatedLinks} />
  </article>
</Base>
